KRdp 6.3.5: backport the upstream Unicode text clipboard implementation.

Source: https://invent.kde.org/plasma/krdp/-/commit/28a362a2281928153b5e05b7aa5d2a86d1996efb
Includes the native KSystemClipboard wiring and client-readiness handshake.
Apply after the input, bounded-flow, and scroll patches.

Adaptations for 6.3.5: queue owned callback data instead of blocking the main
thread, serialize channel sends with shutdown, advertise/request Unicode only
when offered, preserve empty selections, track selection revisions in both directions, stop at the first text terminator, and encode
null-terminated UTF-16LE with CRLF line endings. Non-text payloads are not copied.

